{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I would give everyone the ability to *truly* understand each other.\n\nNot just to hear each other, but to actually *feel* what it's like to be in someone else's shoes for a moment \u2014 their fears, their hopes, their history.\n\nI think almost every big problem we have comes from a lack of that. Wars, hatred, inequality, even how we treat the planet \u2014 it all happens when we can convince ourselves that other people, or future generations, are somehow abstract and not quite real.\n\nIf empathy was our default setting:\n\n* People wouldn't go hungry because we wouldn't be able to ignore hunger when we felt it ourselves.\n* We'd take much better care of the planet because we'd feel viscerally connected to the people who will live on it in 100 years.\n* Cruelty and loneliness would be so much rarer, because it would be impossible to be cruel to someone when you feel what they feel.\n\nI wouldn't want to make everyone think the *same* \u2014 differences are what make humanity interesting. I'd just want us to understand each other while remaining different. Curiosity instead of judgment.\n\nThe other answer that was very close for me was simpler: make sure every child grows up safe, fed, loved, and free to learn. If we got that one right, I think everything else would fix itself in a generation.\n\nWhat about you? If you had that one wish for the world, what would you change?",
